{\color{blue}\qbezier(-4,-1.7)(-4,1.2)(-4,4.1)
\qbezier(-6.5,2)(-2,2)(2.5,2)}
\put(-4,4.25){\makebox(0,0)[b]{$x=-4$}}
\put(2.7,2){$y=2$}
\put(0,-1.25){\makebox(0,0){$\bullet$}}
\put(0.2,-1.25){$(0,-5/4)$}
\end{picture}
\end{center}
\textbf{b)} $f(-3)=-11$ y $f'(x)=13/(x+4)^2$ en el tramo
racional. Así, $f'(-3)=13$ y la tangente
$y+11=13(x+3)$ queda $\boxed{y=13x+28}$.

